Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:58:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(brit-cli): admit the checked read-only commands to
 the closed-reader rule

Each path was read before admission: it writes nothing (a network read
is allowed) and everything it prints goes through `prepare_and_run`'s
watched writers or `output::print_line`. Admitted: `show`, `tag list`,
`remote url|refs|ref-map`, `commit describe`, `revision previous-branches`,
`verify`, `fsck`, `tree entries|info`, `commit-graph list|verify`,
`mailmap entries|check`, `attributes query`, `exclude query`, `submodule`
and `submodule list`, `is-clean`, `is-changed`, `config` and
`config show|list`, `index entries`, `dirwalk`, and `build graph
discover|show`, `affected`, `plan`, `fingerprint`, `baseline read`.

Left out, with the reason beside the list: bare `tag` (creates a tag
when named), `revision list` (`--svg` writes and opens a file), `commit
verify` (runs the verifier and prints through an unwatched stderr),
`attributes validate-baseline` (its git children print past the watched
writer), and every writer.

`is_closed_reader_write()` also recognises JSON that a plumbing command
wrote through `.or_error()` (a `serde_json::Error` inside a `gix::Error`):
`tree info` otherwise ended with "Error: Broken pipe" and 1.

Journey `read_only_closed_reader.rs` (Linux only, it closes a pipe with
libc): every admitted command prints to a live reader, ends with 141 and
an empty stderr when its reader closed first, and the six failing forms
keep their own status. On the base 8e5072ff binary every row fails
(1 with "Error: Broken pipe", 101 for the build commands, 0 for
`index entries`).

